# Window shortcuts (1280x800) on the Text Editor: Super+Right snaps it to the
# right half, Super+Up maximises it, Super+Down restores it, Super+D shows the
# desktop and brings the window back, and Super+Down minimises it. The keys
# come from QEMU's PS/2 keyboard, on the keyboard controller, which the
# driver VM has: Linux's i8042 and atkbd drive it, its ports reached
# through the monitor, its interrupts routed to the guest.
boot-cmdline "run=editor"
wait-serial "started editor" 60
wait-serial "input: AT Translated Set 2 keyboard (i8042 0001:0001): keyboard" 60
expect-serial "serio: i8042 KBD port at 0x60,0x64 irq 1"
wait 6
key meta_l-right
wait 2
shot target/veda/keys-1-right.png
key meta_l-up
wait 2
shot target/veda/keys-2-maximized.png
key meta_l-down
wait 2
shot target/veda/keys-3-restored.png
key meta_l-d
wait 2
shot target/veda/keys-4-desktop.png
key meta_l-d
wait 2
shot target/veda/keys-5-back.png
key meta_l-down
wait 2
shot target/veda/keys-6-minimized.png
reject-serial "touched I/O port"
reject-serial "cannot be routed"
